    "body": "Closes #31706\r\n\r\nAdds `<Plug>(nvim-closewin)`, bound by default to `<M-q>`. It closes the current window like `:close`; if the buffer has a non-empty `'buftype'` (e.g. `:checkhealth`, `:Man`) and is the last window, it closes the buffer instead of failing with `E444`. A normal file in the last window is left as-is.\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-08-16T21:29:45Z",
